If a patient has a chronic-pain and has a depression and a tricyclic-antidepressant is not contraindicated for the patient then every clinician should consider the tricyclic-antidepressant for an analgesic-effect and should consider the tricyclic-antidepressant for an antidepressant-effect.
If a patient has a chronic-pain and has a depression and an SNRI-antidepressant is not contraindicated for the patient then every clinician should consider the SNRI-antidepressant for an analgesic-effect and should consider the SNRI-antidepressant for an antidepressant-effect.
